      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2012 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Witnessing emotional events such as arousal or pain may impair ongoing cognitive processes such as inhibitory control. We found that this may be true only half of the time. Erotic images and painful video clips were shown to men and women shortly before a stop signal task, which measures cognitive inhibitory control. These stimuli impaired inhibitory control only in men and not in women, suggesting that emotional stimuli may be processed with different weights depending on gender."
      },
